View areas (2026-10-14): a browser window that changes shape (a Tesla's own fullscreen 773x601 <-> 1256x706, the
XPeng's fullscreen and dock, split screen) no longer reconnects CarPlay. Each shape the page has shown (at most 4)
becomes a CarPlay view area at the stream's top left, the stream as large as all of them (/info viewAreas,
viewAreaTransitionControl); a shape seen before is reached with updateViewArea {uuid, viewAreaIndex,
animationDurationMillis, adjacentViewAreas} on the event channel, without reconnecting, and the page shows that
area across its view (touches stay in stream coordinates). Only a shape seen the first time, a clearly sharper
size or another codec declares the areas again (one reconnect). The narrowest area keeps the plain icon size: the
display reports 200 mm per that area's width (at 200 mm for the whole 1920 px stream the windowed area looked
crowded). The protocol side follows DiPlay (GPL-3.0, shihabal3amri/DiPlay#246, docs/VIEW_AREAS.md: tested on a
BYD Tang with iOS 27). Replaces "renegotiate a close shape in fullscreen only, once per browser" (2026-10-13).

Tesla, reverse gear: the car froze the browser without hiding the page (the last report a focus loss, then 67 s
of nothing), and afterwards the picture stood still until the page was refreshed. The page now notices it was
frozen (its one-second tick over 4 s late while it was not hidden, or the "resume" event) or that the box went
silent for 8 s while CarPlay runs, and opens the link again at once (Connection.restart leaves a possibly dead
socket without waiting for its close); unlike a reload the sound stays unlocked ("revived" in the viewer log).
A new socket could then hang half-open, the page saying "connecting" until refreshed: one not open within 6 s is
left for another, and after three in a row the page reloads itself, as the person did by hand, but only while
the box answers. A hidden page's slowed timers (the XPeng's reverse camera) are no freeze.
Coming back after the car froze the browser (a Tesla away from it): the iPhone's CarPlay never stops, only the
page's link to the box may. The box pauses a page silent for 3 s (no sound, the picture waits for a keyframe)
and keeps its link 10 minutes; the page, on any sign of coming back (a late tick, focus, pageshow, shown, a touch,
"resume"), asks on its link first and goes on over it with a fresh keyframe when the box answers within 0.6 s, else
opens a new link, which replaces its old one at once (the page's id); a reload only if no link is open 3 s later.
The last picture stays up meanwhile. Logged: viewer connected/paused/resumed/replaced/closed on the box, and the
page's life (ev 8 frozen with gapMs, 9 focus, 10 pageshow, 11 link open again, 12 reloading, 13 back: how 1 same
link, 2 new link).
A link that had been up and is closed (by the box, past 10 minutes) is opened again at once, without back-off.
The last picture is held by awake time only (a timer counting the freeze cleared it the moment the page came back,
just before the new picture), a new link not open within 1.5 s is replaced, and ev 14 reports pictureMs from waking.
A Tesla leaves its Wi-Fi when it leaves Park unless "Remain connected in Drive" is on (6 s off in reverse): on the
browser's "online" event the page opens a new link at once.
Trimmed once the Tesla's Wi-Fi was found to be the cause: no key/wheel/focus diagnostics, the page wakes on a late
tick, shown, resume or online only, a reload only after 15 s without a link, and an open-timer that runs late (the
page frozen meanwhile) gives the socket more time instead of dropping it.
